 "audio_url": null,
 "note_en": "守株待兔 (shǒu zhū dài tù) is a chengyu, a four-character idiom that packs a whole story into four words: \"guard\" + \"tree stump\" + \"wait for\" + \"rabbit.\" Like many chengyu, it works as a moral: 这个成语批评那些不努力、只想靠运气的人 \"This idiom criticizes people who don't work hard and just count on luck.\"",
